{
  "delta_from_prior": "Replaced prior 16-variable fixture (neon_worstcase_auto_00107, which collapsed to peak 1 on v5) and extended Neon58 (20 vars, 108 clauses, 4 lifted vars, mu=2 OR-gate pairs) to a 24-variable, 242-clause, 8-lifted-variable fixture whose 16-variable, 52-clause exact quotient adds 4 circularly shifted positive cross-clauses (a_i v b_{i+1} v c_i v d_{i+1}). This exercises width-8 local-certificate compression at 24 variables, keeps core_refutation UNKNOWN on both original and quotient, preserves peak >= 8 on v5 without adding width-5 IALH union windows, and raises every 2-variable cell cofactor count from mu=2 to mu=4 to defeat Fable73 link-twin contraction and Fable97 CELL/bmw at |C|=2.",
  "explanation": "1. CODE AUDIT OF PINNED v5 (NO EXECUTION CLAIMED)\nAuditing the supplied v5 solver, compression.py, core_refutation.py, and pinned dependencies (check_scc_and_growth.py, test_elim.py, test_mra.py) revealed no soundness bug yielding a wrong SAT decision:\n- compression.py (_verify_certificate): partitions every dense original clause into exact-support blocks, checks block_clause_counts sums to len(quotient), rejects any quotient form whose support escapes the block mask (forms[i] & ~mask), verifies evaluate(clauses, x) == evaluate(q, image) over all 2^|support| local assignments, and checks P*L = I_r entrywise over GF(2) (proving surjectivity). No omitted-block bug is present.\n- core_refutation.py (probe): enforces set(core).issubset(set(f)) independently and only refutes when compress_root(core) succeeds with an UNSAT 2-SAT quotient; SAT/UNKNOWN/non-binary always falls back. Applying probe once to an exact quotient preserves soundness.\n- ialh5 / residual solver: verify_certificate rebuilds UP tables from the normalized formula and verifies uA in Z^m, ub not in Z using exact Fraction arithmetic; canon_plus (UP + subsumption + signed SCC), elim_plus (size-nonincreasing DP), two_sat, and prune (syntactic subsumption) are sound.\n- Prior receipts acknowledged: neon_worstcase_auto_00107 collapsed to observed peak 1 on v5 (not confirmed), and Neon54/55 were falsified as growth witnesses (peak 0 via globally combined IALH-5 congruences).\n\nOperational weakness exploited: compress_root sorts candidate forms by (-block_frequency, popcount, bitmask), and run_counting passes variables(quotient) in ascending order to run_counting_core. Whenever all basis forms share the same block frequency, weight-1 unlifted variables are deterministically placed before weight-2 XOR-lifted variables in the quotient order.\n\n2. CONSTRUCTION OF THE 24-VARIABLE, 242-CLAUSE GROWTH FIXTURE\nVariables 1..24 compress exactly to 16 quotient variables representing four Left pairs P_i = {a_i, b_i} and four Right pairs Q_j = {c_j, d_j} (i,j in 1..4):\n- Weight-1 unlifted forms: 1=a1, 2=c1, 3=a2, 4=c2, 5=a3, 6=c3, 7=a4, 8=c4.\n- Weight-2 XOR-lifted forms: b1=9^10, d1=11^12, b2=13^14, d2=15^16, b3=17^18, d3=19^20, b4=21^22, d4=23^24.\n\nThe 52 quotient clauses (all width 4, all with distinct supports) are:\n- Group 1 (16 negative L-clauses -> 81 original clauses, widths 4..8): all (~u1 v ~u2 v ~u3 v ~u4) for u_i in {a_i, b_i}. Forces some P_i = (0,0).\n- Group 2 (16 negative R-clauses -> 81 original clauses, widths 4..8): all (~w1 v ~w2 v ~w3 v ~w4) for w_j in {c_j, d_j}. Forces some Q_j = (0,0).\n- Group 3 (16 positive cross-clauses -> 64 original clauses, width 6): (a_i v b_i v c_j v d_j) for all i,j in 1..4. Forbids P_i = (0,0) and Q_j = (0,0) simultaneously.\n- Group 4 (4 circularly shifted positive cross-clauses -> 16 original clauses, width 6): (a_i v b_{i+1} v c_i v d_{i+1}) for i=1..4 (indices mod 4).\n\nTotal: 24 variables, 242 clauses, max width 8.\n\n3. EXACT COMPRESSION, CORE REFUTATION, UNSAT, AND SAT CONTROL\n- Compression (not a skip): only the 2 unlifted blocks (~a1 v ~a2 v ~a3 v ~a4) and (~c1 v ~c2 v ~c3 v ~c4) have odd size (8 frozen vars < 24). Total local space points = 1296 + 1296 + 1024 + 256 = 3872 <= 16384; verification work is ~5e5 << 8e6; max block width 8 <= 8. Every intended basis form has exact block frequency 13 (8 neg + 4 cross + 1 shifted), while every non-basis sum has frequency <= 5. Thus greedy selection is guaranteed compatible and yields the exact 16-var, 52-clause quotient in order [a1, c1, a2, c2, a3, c3, a4, c4, b1, d1, b2, d2, b3, d3, b4, d4].\n- Core refutation: on the original formula, every block is a single exact coset of its stabilizer subspace, so counts[v] is either |z| or 0 and 0 clauses are removed (UNKNOWN: no_clauses_removed). On the 52-clause quotient, every clause has a unique support (block size 1), so 0 clauses are removed (UNKNOWN: no_clauses_removed).\n- UNSAT and nearby SAT control: Groups 1-3 alone form the UNSAT bipartite 4-pair transversal contradiction, so adding Group 4 preserves UNSAT. Deleting the single original clause [-1, -3, -5, -7] (i.e. (~a1 v ~a2 v ~a3 v ~a4)) makes the formula SAT: set a1=a2=a3=a4=1 (satisfying all positive clauses in Groups 3-4 and all remaining negative L-clauses except the deleted one), b_i=0, c1=d1=0, c2=d2=c3=d3=c4=d4=1.\n\n4. RESIDUAL GROWTH ON v5 AND COUNTEREXAMPLE TO FABLE97 CELL/bmw\n- Residual growth on v5: at the root and first three branching layers (a1, c1, a2), all clauses have width >= 3, no unit/SCC/2-SAT reductions occur, every width-<=5 UP table retains >= 15/16 points (integer affine hull Z^|W|, zero IALH rows), and every active variable has pos >= 4, neg >= 2 (elim_plus stuck). All 8 branches of (a1, c1, a2) are pairwise incomparable under syntactic subsumption (peak >= 8). Crucially, each Group 4 shifted clause shares at most 2 variables with any other quotient clause (union size >= 6 > k=5), adding zero width-5 union windows and only 4 width-4 windows to IALH-5, keeping runtime close to Neon58.\n- Counterexample to Fable73 link-twins and Fable97 CELL/bmw: in Neon58, each pair {a_i, b_i} had only mu=2 syntactic cofactor classes (pure OR-gate a_i v b_i), allowing Fable73/Fable97 to collapse 16 variables to 8 and pair-adjacent ordering to reduce peak from 8 to 2. With Group 4, a_i appears in (a_i v b_{i+1} v c_i v d_{i+1}) without b_i, and b_i appears in (a_{i-1} v b_i v c_{i-1} v d_i) without a_i. Consequently, for every pair {a_i, b_i} (and similarly {c_j, d_j}), the four assignments (0,0), (0,1), (1,0), (1,1) yield four distinct syntactic cofactors (mu=4). Every non-paired 2-variable cell also has disjoint clause incidences, so EVERY 2-variable cell in the 16-variable quotient has mu=4 (zero bit reduction under link-twin contraction or CELL/bmw at |C|=2), and the circular coupling breaks the (0,1)/(1,0)/(1,1) subsumption collapse under pair-adjacent branching order.\n\nScope note: this is a finite 24-variable witness and hand derivation, not an asymptotic lower bound.",
